        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most leaking gutters, Geocel 2320 is the sealant to buy. It is made for gutter seams, bonds to every common gutter material and tolerates damp metal. Add a tube of Geocel 2300 if you have vertical downspout joints to seal, keep Sashco Through the Roof on hand for repairs that cannot wait for dry weather, and choose DAP Butyl-Flex if budget matters most and you can work on a dry day.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Whatever you buy, the prep decides the result. Clear the gutter, scrape out the old sealant, brush the joint to bright metal, rivet anything loose and seal from the inside. And if the gutter is rusting through, cracking or sagging, spend the money on a new section instead of another tube.
